==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|cazic|cazique}}

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|es|cacique}}, from {{der|en|tnq|*kasike}} or {{der|en|arw|kassequa}}, {{m|arw|cazaqah||chieftain; power}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|historical}} A [[tribal chief]] in the [[Spanish]] [[West Indies]].
#: {{syn|en|chieftain}}
#* {{quote-journal
|en
|title=Why Mexico Has Only One Big Hat In the Ring
|date=Dec. 5, 1993
|author=Anthony Depalma
|work=New York Times
|url=https://www.nytimes.com/1993/12/05/weekinreview/the-world-why-mexico-has-only-one-big-hat-in-the-ring.html
|passage=Mexico has loved a strong leader since before Moctezuma. Indigenous tribes were ruled by '''caciques''', or chieftans{{sic}}, and in some rural communities '''caciques''' are still unchallenged.}}
# A [[local]] [[political]] [[leader]] in [[Latin America]], [[Spain]], or the [[Philippines]].
#: {{cot|en|caudillo}}
# {{lb|en|ornithology}} Any of a number of [[tropical]] [[blackbird]]s from [[Central America]] and [[South America]], family {{l|mul|Icteridae}}.

